@inzamam-iqbal thanks for the independent trace — confirmed, and your diagnosis matches exactly.

The code fix landed in `6ecfab6`: `Glm4MoeMTPModel`, `Glm4MoeLiteMTPModel`, `GlmOcrMTPModel` are now in the `model_returns_tuple()` set, so the `SpecDecodeBaseProposer` path (Model Runner V1 / `VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER=0`) unpacks the `(post, post)` tuple instead of indexing it at L614 — including at `num_speculative_tokens=1`, as you note. (The MRV2 worker speculators were already fine since they unpack via `isinstance`.)

On the test placement — thanks for pointing it out. it is updated in `c4a5b66`: extended the parametrization of `test_mtp_model_returns_tuple` in `tests/v1/spec_decode/test_llm_base_proposer_sampling.py` (the CPU spec-decode CI job) with the three GLM architectures, and dropped the equivalent ad-hoc test I'd added to `test_mtp.py`. I also kept a proposer-level `test_mtp_propose` extended to `num_speculative_tokens ∈ {1, 2}` × `{single-tensor, tuple}` returns for the integration coverage @larryli2-amd asked about.

